.TH CUT 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
cut \- remove sections from each line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cut
\fB\-d\fR \fIDELIM\fR \fB\-f\fR \fILIST\fR [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print selected, delimiter-separated fields from each line of FILE (standard input by default).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d \fIDELIM\fR
Use DELIM as the field delimiter (default: tab).
.TP
.B \-f \fILIST\fR
Comma-separated field numbers and ranges, e.g. \fB1,3\-5\fR.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH NOTES
Field selection is by delimiter only -- \fB\-c\fR (character ranges) and \fB\-b\fR (byte ranges) are not supported.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
